# Exact quantum reference for Tully model I (simple avoided crossing).
#
# Grid-based nonadiabatic wavepacket propagation on the same diabatic
# Hamiltonian: A=0.01, B=1.6, C=0.005, D=1.0, reduced mass 2000 a.u. The packet
# starts on the lower adiabatic surface at x=-6 moving right; the populations
# below are converged to five decimals over the last output points.
#
# Produced by validation/tully/wavepacket, which is the code from this Dropbox
# library rebuilt with two corrections: an off-by-one in the FFT momentum grid,
# and double precision throughout. See wavepacket/CHANGES.md.
#
# The number of steps is chosen per momentum so the packet never reaches the
# periodic boundary. This matters: the earlier saved runs used a fixed step
# count, and at k=30 and above the packet wrapped around and re-entered from
# the far side, which corrupted the result. A previously recorded value of
# 0.44392 at k=45.166 was contaminated this way; the clean value is 0.85871.
#
# k_ini   nstep   population_lower   population_upper
   8.000   4000       0.93896            0.06104
  10.000   4000       0.84479            0.15521
  12.000   4000       0.78124            0.21876
  15.000   4000       0.67696            0.32304
  20.000   4000       0.50699            0.49301
  30.000   2000       0.28572            0.71428
  45.166   1200       0.14129            0.85871
